# real-estate-voice-agent - Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to server/.env and fill it in:
#
#     cp server/.env.example server/.env
#
# This file MUST live next to bot.py. bot.py resolves its .env by walking up
# from its own directory, so a .env at the repo root is silently ignored while
# server/.env wins. Keep exactly one .env, here.
#
# Everything under "Required" is validated at boot. There are no code-level
# defaults, on purpose: a hardcoded fallback turns a missing value into a
# confusing runtime API error minutes later instead of a named failure now.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Google AI Studio, https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Gemini model id. NOTE: the ListModels endpoint advertises models that
# generateContent rejects with 404, so verify any value here with a real
# generateContent call before trusting it. Known good on 2026-07-28:
# gemini-3.5-flash-lite (fastest), gemini-flash-lite-latest, gemini-3.6-flash.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Deepgram, https://console.deepgram.com
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs, https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs voice id. A Voice Library voice must be ADDED to your account
# first, otherwise the API reports it as nonexistent rather than unauthorized.
# List the voices actually on your account:
#   curl -s -H "xi-api-key: $ELEVENLABS_API_KEY" https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/voices
# EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL is Sarah, a stock voice available to every account.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL

# --- Required only for the twilio transport ---------------------------------
# Not needed for `uv run bot.py -t webrtc`.

TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio rates are deliberately SPLIT. Input stays at 8 kHz so STT accuracy in
# the browser matches what the phone line will give you. Output is 16 kHz
# because ElevenLabs PCM formats are 16000, 22050, 24000 and 44100.
# Raise AUDIO_IN_SAMPLE_RATE only to hear how the agent sounds without the
# telephony bandwidth limit. Never tune VAD against it.

# AUDIO_IN_SAMPLE_RATE=8000
# AUDIO_OUT_SAMPLE_RATE=16000

# How long the smart turn analyzer waits, after the caller goes quiet, before
# ending their turn anyway. Pipecat's default is 3. Measured on 2026-07-29,
# two of six turns hit that ceiling exactly and cost 3.2 seconds each.
#
# Lower is snappier AND interrupts callers who pause mid-sentence more often.
# There is no correct value, only the one that sounds right. Change it here,
# hold a conversation on -t webrtc, then compare with `uv run latency.py`:
# the `user turn` row's max should fall toward whatever you set.

# SMART_TURN_STOP_SECS=1.5
